WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.540
Do you live around here?

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.210
It's all right, we're not your enemy!

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.610
We're looking for a place where we can unwind.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.600
If there's a village, could you lead us there?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.180
Sorry about this.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.200
Base here. What's wrong?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.470
We're currently about 200 meters from G Nest.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.470
We haven't seen a single Blue around here.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.100
There are no Blue?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.720
According to X-ray camera investigation,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.150
the hardness of the outer walls is about 200.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.820
And to make things worse...

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:54.830
...there's nothing like an entrance anywhere along the outer walls.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.830
It is expected that securing an infiltration route will be extremely difficult.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:03.500
Understood. Take it easy, and find yourself a suitable place to rest.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.500
Roger. We will do just that.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.840
What do we do?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.480
With the Armor Shrikes, it won't even take half a day to reach the Nest.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.540
It's not very fair to the villagers,

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.510
but we'll make our base here for a while.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:19.050
That's fine. Seeing as how there are people living here,

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.520
you know that there is enough to eat!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.890
In the worst case, if we're short on combat supplies,

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:30.530
there won't be much trouble turning back to the shuttle and all...

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.800
It's better than nothing at all.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.800
Nothing at all, huh?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.070
Yuji, doesn't it strike you as being a little strange?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:45.480
The scouting party says that there are no Blue around the Nest...

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:50.720
Yeah, we haven't encountered a single Blue yet.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.150
And yet, how come there's that gigantic Nest here in a place like this?

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.890
It's our job to investigate that too.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.790
It's been three months.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.230
What in the world is happening now on Earth?

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.840
What's that? The Blue on the surface have started to migrate?

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.040
Look at this.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:20.180
These are the latest images of the surface that have been sent by our surveillance satellite.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.010
It's thought that the Blue

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:26.850
were born to eliminate the continually multiplying humankind.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:32.390
The existence of many more Blue in urban areas was also thought to make it more convenient

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.460
for them to fulfill their role.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:39.030
However, suddenly, there are more Blue existing elsewhere.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:44.470
What is seen as unusual are those Blue that are inhabiting those areas out in nature.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:48.440
You can see that the Blue all over South America are migrating,

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.810
heading to one spot.

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.810
South America... The Guyanan highlands!?

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:58.250
Why are they now headed toward the Guyanan highlands?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.820
What exactly does it mean?

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:07.490
I am guessing that this could be a harbinger of what other changes will occur on Earth.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:11.500
- Harbinger of changes?
- What does that mean?

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.730
At this current stage, we cannot be certain of anything.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:19.700
Supposing that something has happened, I don't think that we,

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.170
living here in space, have any particular influence over it.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:24.840
I'm going!

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:29.180
In any case, somebody has to go down and verify this, right?

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:33.780
I will go and see what is happening on Earth with my own eyes for you!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.220
Yuji...

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.360
I will provide you with the necessary supplies.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.800
You should recruit volunteers and put together a unit. However...

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.000
...afterward, no matter what is occurring,

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.900
it will be no concern of ours.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.800
If our communications with you are lost,

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.810
we're cutting off all contact with Earth.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:58.910
That's fine. I wasn't planning on coming back here in the first place.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.810
After all, there's no room on this station for a Sleeper.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.150
Let's go, Marlene.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.820
Right...

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:12.850
We will find for ourselves the road down which we will live!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.500
I never even tried to imagine it...

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.600
Being here like this, it seems crazy that up until now,

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.830
I've lived up there.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.430
Marlene...

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.740
No matter what happens, I am here with you, Yuji.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.780
I was just thinking...

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:38.840
<i>I wish this moment</i> <i>could last forever.</i>

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:49.780
Yuji...?

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.000
Are you okay?

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.150
If you're fetching water, I'll go with you.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:15.140
You show me where the water is, okay?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.250
H- hey...!

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:46.120
<i>If only all people could</i> <i>live like these children...</i>

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.240
Marlene!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.590
What's this?

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.820
Blasting operations complete.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.160
Status?

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:32.500
No good. There's no damage to the outer wall.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.500
I see...

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.500
Looks like forcing our way through is hopeless.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.500
Shall we increase the charge and try from a different direction?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:43.170
No, there's no sense in wasting the explosives.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:45.840
Let's try thinking of some other way.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.510
- Roger.
- But when you talk about some other way...

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:53.520
That's the problem right there.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.680
Yuji!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:08.870
A giant road in the middle of the forest?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.400
The people in the village said they saw it.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.930
A great deal of Blue moved through the forest and disappeared into the valley.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.220
There's a valley ahead of here?

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:29.220
But this is quite a ways off from the direction of the Nest.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.220
About how long ago are we talking?

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:35.130
According to what the children said, about three months ago.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.160
That coincides with the time of the Blue mass migration

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.490
observed by the surveillance satellite.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.870
My, my, we're leaving already?

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:20.200
And here I thought we were going to be able to live like humans for a little bit.

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:27.210
Now that you mention it,

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:30.710
Ted, you're a Sleeper that woke up on the station, right?

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.150
Would you mind telling us...

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:34.490
...about the life you used to lead in the past, Ted?

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:37.150
Hm? Sure...

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:41.030
I was raised in rural Texas, see? On this huge sprawling ranch.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:46.160
I spent long days there, living my life driving cattle.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:07.150
Thinking back now, I lived pretty casually then.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:11.190
If I could, I'd sure like to go back to that time.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:14.530
Whether we can go back or not...

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:15.960
...all depends on this.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:31.210
An underground path?

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:33.770
Does this go through to the Nest?

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:40.180
Yuji...

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:47.490
<i>I'm sure that ahead of us, there must</i> <i>be something that we want to know.</i>

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:52.000
Infantry and vehicles 8 through 12 stay here on stand-by.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:57.190
If after six hours, if nobody returns, pull back to the village.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.230
Let's go!

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.590
This is eerie!

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:18.190
Looks like this might continue all the way down to the bottom of Hell.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.850
All units, equip night scopes.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.770
I- It's the Blue!!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:37.810
Relax!!

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.740
Calm down, Ted! Look closely!!

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.610
Man, don't scare me like that!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.320
Yuji, look at that.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.740
Ew... What is all this?

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.580
That is nasty!

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.190
Is this...

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:27.520
...a Blue graveyard?

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:33.130
Graveyard...!? Is this another "Planned Suicide?"

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.330
What do you mean by that?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:43.840
The Blue were born in order to eliminate mankind,

00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:47.280
who were breeding without bounds.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:54.150
Supposing they were to accomplish their goal, then instead of mankind,

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.150
the Blue themselves would then be the ones breeding,

00:16:56.150 --> 00:17:00.560
and to the Earth, they would be the ones whose existence was unessential.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.800
And so, it was necessary for them to go extinct themselves.

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:11.840
They were already programmed to do this.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.170
I see. Which means...?

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:19.940
The "Planned Suicide" over the Earth is near its end.

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:23.040
Is that unthinkable, Yuji?

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.520
Yuji?

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:29.950
The "Planned Suicide"...is over?

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.130
No... What is this!?

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:40.130
Ted, can you feel it? Like this...

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:43.130
...incredibly strong... some kind of power!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:47.470
Huh? P- power, you say?

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.140
What's the matter, Yuji?

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.140
- I can feel it!
- Feel what?

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:56.370
I don't know... But I feel it. I feel a strong power!

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:27.510
Sensing a large-scale tremor in the northern area of South America.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.880
Measuring M7.8 on the seismic scale.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:32.450
The quake's center is in the eastern Guyanan highlands!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:37.410
Scout party, this is the military station! Report your situation!

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.930
Oh, shit!

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.360
Marlene!

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.920
Marlene... Marlene!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.830
Ted! Ted!?

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.830
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.300
Yuji, look!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:26.900
What's that?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.140
Let's go!

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:03.140
Let's go? H- hey!

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:05.630
Hold on, now! Yuji!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.440
What!?

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.190
Yuji!

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:32.400
W- what is that!?

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.340
It's not over!

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:55.480
You intend to not let us through!?

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:02.990
Are we that much of an inconvenience to you!?

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:38.460
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:44.590
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:53.740
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:59.910
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:06.330
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:13.520
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:18.680
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:24.740
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:31.020
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:38.500
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:45.360
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:49.980
<i>What do we do, Yuji?</i>

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:52.640
<i>Are we that much of an</i> <i>inconvenience to you!?</i>

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:54.310
<i>Let's go, together...</i>

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:56.320
<i>This is where we part, Marlene.</i>

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:57.650
<i>Yuji?</i>

00:22:57.650 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>Marlene, I want you</i> <i>at least to stay alive.</i>

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:03.490
<i>In that case, more than</i> <i>ever, let's stay together!</i>

00:23:03.490 --> 00:23:06.990
<i>Come back with me. For the</i> <i>sake of our unborn child.</i>

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:09.460
<i>So that I may live</i> <i>together with you, Marlene,</i>

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:12.090
<i>and everyone else, I'm going!</i>
